This is a focused corrective pass for the combat Knockback architecture.

The current implementation misunderstands how Knockback is supposed to work.

This distinction is extremely important:

THERE ARE TWO DIFFERENT SYSTEMS

1. DEFAULT KNOCKBACK / ATTACK KNOCKBACK

Every attack has its own built-in launch strength.

This answers:

“How hard does this move naturally knock someone away?”

Examples:

* a small push should have weak default knockback;
* BA1 should have its own default launch;
* BA2 can have stronger default launch;
* #0001’s Sphere Rush explosion should have very strong default horizontal launch;
* shuriken can have zero default launch.

This property belongs to the attack.

It represents the attack’s inherent physical force.

⸻

2. ACCUMULATED KNOCKBACK

Every fighter has a separate accumulated Knockback number.

This starts at:

0

When the fighter takes damage, that damage is added to this number.

Examples:

* fighter starts at 0;
* BA1 deals 5 damage → accumulated Knockback becomes 5;
* another BA1 → 10;
* BA2 deals 10 → 20;
* etc.

This answers:

“How vulnerable to being launched has this fighter become?”

The higher this number gets, the more additional launch the fighter receives from hits.

This property belongs to the fighter being hit, not the attack.

⸻

3. These are NOT the same thing

Do not treat:

attack default knockback

and:

fighter accumulated Knockback

as one value.

Do not refer to them interchangeably.

They are two separate parts of final launch.

A strong attack is strong because its own default knockback is strong.

A damaged fighter flies farther because their accumulated Knockback creates additional launch.

Both matter.

⸻

4. Current implementation problem

The repository currently uses logic conceptually equivalent to:

finalLaunch = attackBaseLaunch * (1 + accumulatedKnockback / 100)

This is the wrong model.

It makes accumulated Knockback completely dependent on the attack’s base/default knockback.

That means accumulated Knockback is only acting as a multiplier of the attack.

This is exactly what must be corrected.

Remove this architecture.

Specifically inspect:

* js/data/knockback.js
* knockbackMultiplier()
* scaleKnockback()
* js/game/combat.js
* CombatSystem.applyHit()
* tests that assert launch multiplier behavior
* README / ALVA_SPEC comments describing multiplier behavior.

⸻

5. Correct conceptual formula

Final launch must have two independent components:

final launch = attack default launch + accumulated-Knockback bonus launch

The first term comes from the attack.

The second term comes from the target’s accumulated Knockback.

Do not calculate the second term by multiplying the first.

Conceptually:

finalX = defaultX + accumulatedBonusX

finalY = defaultY + accumulatedBonusY

The accumulated bonus should use the attack’s launch direction, but not its default magnitude.

This distinction is critical.

⸻

6. Direction and strength are separate

An attack still decides what direction it launches.

Examples:

* horizontal hit → accumulated Knockback bonus also pushes horizontally;
* upward launcher → accumulated Knockback bonus also goes upward;
* downward spike → accumulated Knockback bonus also goes downward.

But the size of the accumulated-Knockback contribution is determined from the fighter’s accumulated Knockback value independently.

The attack tells the system:

which way

The accumulated Knockback number tells the system:

how much additional launch susceptibility

The attack’s default knockback tells the system:

how hard this move inherently hits

⸻

