8. Why this distinction matters

The default attack knockback exists specifically so attacks can have different natural strength.

For example:

* a shove;
* a normal punch;
* a launcher;
* a powerful explosion

should not have identical launch at zero accumulated Knockback.

Likewise, accumulated Knockback exists so a heavily damaged fighter becomes increasingly easy to launch regardless of whether the incoming move’s own default knockback is Low, Mid, High, or bespoke.

The two systems complement each other.

One must not numerically derive the other.

