25. Suggested helper behavior

Conceptually:

resolveLaunch(base, accumulated)

If base is zero:

return { x: 0, y: 0 }

Otherwise:

Horizontal base

If:

base.x !== 0

calculate:

extraX = horizontalBonus(accumulated)

then:

finalX = sign(base.x) * (abs(base.x) + extraX)

Y stays based on existing Y behavior.

Vertical base

If:

base.y !== 0

calculate:

extraY = verticalBonus(accumulated)

then:

finalY = sign(base.y) * (abs(base.y) + extraY)

This means accumulated Knockback increases magnitude without deciding direction.

