56. Acceptance criteria

This correction is complete when:

Architecture

* default attack knockback and accumulated Knockback are clearly separate concepts;
* no gameplay launch multiplier remains;
* accumulated Knockback is not multiplied by attack base force;
* final launch is base/default launch plus an independent accumulated contribution.

Attack identity

* Low/Mid/High remain attack properties;
* bespoke strong attacks remain possible;
* Sphere Rush explosion remains much stronger by default than a push;
* zero-launch attacks remain zero-launch.

Accumulation

* damage still adds to target Knockback;
* target Knockback stays a plain numeric value;
* higher accumulated Knockback causes stronger launch;
* no hard cap is added unless one already exists elsewhere.

Direction

* attack determines launch direction;
* accumulated Knockback only increases magnitude in that direction;
* horizontal stays horizontal;
* upward stays upward;
* downward stays downward;
* zero-launch hits remain zero.

Code

* knockbackMultiplier() no longer drives combat;
* scaleKnockback() multiplicative behavior is removed/replaced;
* applyHit() combines base launch + accumulated bonus;
* launchMultiplier event field is removed/replaced;
* comments/docs no longer describe multiplicative scaling.

Tests

* weak and strong attacks receive the same accumulated bonus at the same target Knockback;
* their original default strength difference remains;
* shuriken remains zero-launch at high accumulated Knockback;
* CAB2 ticks remain zero-launch;
* CAB2 explosion uses strong base + independent accumulated horizontal bonus;
* damage and default knockback are tested independently;
* old multiplier assertions are removed;
* complete test suite passes.

